ts><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIE TAKESHI</name> <address><country>JP</country> </address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NODA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUDA TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NODA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUDA, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIE TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NODA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUDA TOSHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NODA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUDA, TOSHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A cell comprising a negative electrode (11) and a positive electrode (12) which are oppositely disposed through an electrolyte (13). The electrolyte (13) comprises a material obtained by polymerizing a composition comprising a compound having an ether bond and a cross-linkable functional group, a siloxane derivative, and a lithium salt. Through polymerization, the compound having an ether bond and a cross-linkable group forms a three-dimensional network structure. The derivative and the salt are present in the network structure. Thus, ionic conductivity can be heightened while retaining high film-forming properties and high film strength.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cellule comportant une électrode (11) négative et une électrode (12) positive qui sont placées en opposition à travers un électrolyte (13). L'électrolyte (13) comporte une matière obtenue par polymérisation d'une composition comprenant un composé qui possède une liaison éther et un groupe fonctionnel réticulable, un dérivé de siloxane et un sel de lithium. Après polymérisation, le composé possédant une liaison éther et un groupe réticulable forme une structure réticulaire tridimensionnelle. Le dérivé et le sel sont présents dans la structure réticulaire. On peut ainsi augmenter la conductivité ionique tout en maintenant des propriétés filmogènes élevées et une résistance de film élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>